-- Migration (system): identity integrity slice S-2a (docs/IDENTITY-INTEGRITY-PLAN.md section 5; owner decisions OD-1 and OD-2). Forward-only and ADDITIVE: two NULLable columns and one check on the user table. Nothing existing is
-- dropped, replaced, disabled or modified, nothing is seeded and no setting is touched. Opaque physical names (D-029) are generated by tools/schema/system-user-tag.cjs (logical dictionary: SystemSchema.UserTag.cs). Do not edit by hand.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS: the user row carries a key id and a MAC (the tag) over its security fields, computed by the API with a key the database does not hold: login, the session lookup and the enrolment paths refuse a user whose tag does
-- not verify. A row without a tag is not honoured (no compatibility mode, OD-2): the one-time owner tagging command tags the existing users. The database cannot verify a MAC; it enforces only the shape of the two columns.

ALTER TABLE t_fc83d26e
    ADD COLUMN c_bd7bf28a varchar(32) NULL,
    ADD COLUMN c_b07014bb bytea NULL,
    ADD CONSTRAINT k_459ef18b CHECK ((c_bd7bf28a IS NULL AND c_b07014bb IS NULL)
        OR (c_bd7bf28a ~ '^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$' AND octet_length(c_b07014bb) = 32));
